## 2) Extra 2.9 probes (independent of harness; same host)
Ephemeral fixtures: `/tmp/s29_integration/probes/` (not repo root). Same host ELF. `timeout 15s`.

| Probe | check | emit-c | Read |
|-------|-------|--------|------|
| stmt `println(tok)` SECRET | rc=1 `ERR secret` `println sink refuses SECRET tok` | rc=1 same | front-door token walker **TP** |
| stmt `eprintln(tok)` SECRET | rc=1 `ERR secret` `eprintln sink refuses SECRET tok` | rc=1 same | same front-door (`sid == eprintln`) |
| stmt `println(1, tok)` | rc=1 `ERR secret` println | rc=1 same | multi-arg IDENT still walked |
| stmt `eprintln(1, tok)` | rc=1 `ERR secret` eprintln | rc=1 same | same |
| `let f = println; f(tok)` | rc=1 `ERR secret` println | rc=1 same | alias resolve in token walker (2.4) |
| `let f = eprintln; f(tok)` | rc=1 `ERR secret` eprintln | rc=1 same | same |
| `let r = eprintln(tok)` | rc=1 `ERR secret` eprintln | rc=1 same | expr form still front-door |
| `println("tok")` / `eprintln("tok")` | rc=0 `OK` | rc=0 | no-FP (STRING ≠ IDENT) |
| `log(tok)` SECRET | rc=1 `ERR type` `undefined variable 'log'` | rc=1 `ERR secret` `log sink refuses SECRET tok` | **emit-guard path** (log **not** in L175–192 walker); check type-first |
| `print_err(tok)` SECRET | rc=1 `ERR type` `undefined variable 'print_err'` | rc=1 `ERR secret` `print_err sink refuses SECRET tok` | same split |

`check_secret_println_sinks` is invoked from `c_emit.oo` L86 **before** lower. SECRET IDENT on `println`/`eprintln` therefore **never reaches** `c_secret_emit_guard` on emit-c — the token walker `process_exit`s first. Live eprintln refuse is **not** proof that stmt println was unified.

`log` / `print_err` are **not** in the L175–192 println/eprintln token branch. emit-c continues to `c_emit_expr_c` → `c_secret_emit_guard` → `c_guard_scan_idents` and refuses. That is the **existing** emit-guard rail for sibling sinks. `oodac check` on this host typechecks first and never prints `ERR secret` for those names.

Stmt `println` after a clean front-door still lowers via `c_emit_println` (`c_secret_refuse_println_ident`, `__sec__` only — **no** alias resolve at that belt). Alias refuse is the front-door `c_secret_resolve_alias` + `c_secret_refuse_sink_resolved`. Unifying to `c_secret_emit_guard` would put alias + C-text scan on one helper; that land has **not** happened.

